WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.510
Hallsands, South Devon: a fishing
village on a rock ledge in Start Bay.

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.870
For decades, a shingle beach
protected its houses from the waves.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:16.350
On 26 January 1917, a violent storm and
spring tides sent waves crashing into

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.650
the houses.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.330
By 28 January, the village was destroyed.

6
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.070
All 79 villagers survived.

7
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.350
A local newspaper blamed a naval dockyard.

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.350
Bigger waves from its ships?

9
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.110
Why blame a dockyard?

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.250
In this mission, you'll map
Start Bay as a sediment cell,

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.170
and find out where its shingle came from.

12
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:42.190
Then you'll follow the chain of
events, from 1895 to the coast today.

13
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.090
Your mission: explain why a local newspaper
blamed a naval dockyard for the loss

14
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.270
of Hallsands.
